{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>But I will give it, etc. a land flowing, etc.</b> It is difficult: after it said ״לָרֶשֶׁת אוֹתָהּ״ (to possess it), what need is there to say ״וַאֲנִי אֶתְּנֶנָּה״ (but I will give it)? Further, why did it attach the praise of the land to the mention of the inheritance? And it appears to me that the intention is that besides what they will inherit, He will further grant them that the land will flow with milk and honey more than the measure it had previously, and also as spoil not during the time of their inheritance thereafter — which is the time of destruction — that it not be flowing with milk and honey, as those who know it have recounted in this time, due to our sins."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:59:55.139227596Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}